WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:17.440
This is a way to create visibility.

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:25.000
Especially, to show what I do,
in my case, in the dance field,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.200
and what I've been learning
throughout the years.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:33.320
This is my culture, I can confront it
and make it visible.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:37.040
This way I can also work with people

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:43.200
that can help me to expand.
I also have the opportunity to go abroad

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.360
and work with people
from many different countries.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:54.240
Through this Lab we can meet other artists
from different countries

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:59.280
and diverse backgrounds and skills.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:04.920
We can share and see how do they do
and I can show my skills too.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:16.760
How do you communicate using
the strength of each person.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:20.640
Some people were sitting in a wheelchair
but it doesn't matter,

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:25.200
there are always possibilites
to work with the situation,

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.640
to work with a wheelchair,
to work with a person,

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:33.240
to work with the environment,
with everything you see,

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:36.200
everything that you can use
to make your piece.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:41.760
It's very rare but also rich
to have such a diverse group together

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:44.800
during the artistic Lab this week.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:49.600
And that means so much for
the development of all these artists,

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:52.040
their talent development.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:56.480
And therefore, I think it's very important
that these artistic Labs are happening.

00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:00.720
It helps every single one of them

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:04.400
to go back to their own place
and develop even further.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:09.680
It's been about heightening
choreographers' senses, I would say,

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:13.320
and that's been quite key,
just sensing

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:18.920
what's going on in the space
and how you are working with your partner.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:22.680
I think that's really important.
And what's really interesting

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:26.840
is it feels like this course is something
that every choreographer should do, actually.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:29.800
It's something that everyone should practice.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:37.520
I'm most interested when I see work

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:40.240
that's coming from

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:45.280
some new or strange or unexpected
perspective.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.840
For me, this is the point of art.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:53.200
That we reimagine how we're living,
what we care about, what we do.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:57.080
And I think...
I can only speak from my own perspective,

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:00.520
but I think living in a world

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:06.720
with a very particular experience,
if the world makes you immediately question:

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:09.480
"does this have to be like this?",

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:11.520
"are there different ways?".

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:17.760
And so, I think all the artists at this Lab
are pushing the edges

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:24.400
of what is the expectation of their work,
what else is possible.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:30.880
And I think that any artist who comes
with a very unusual perspective on the world

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:35.640
has a lot to offer
and makes the most interesting work.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:50.560
For me, it's about individuals having voices,
and really strong voices,

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:54.600
and being present and not being ignored
nor sidetracked.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:59.040
So, that's the key for me,
is that there are voices in the room

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:03.480
and they are being noticed.
And it's acceptable that they are different

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:06.120
and we celebrate the differences.

